Pro-Level Insight (Important for your scale)

Since you mentioned hundreds of resources earlier, doing terraform state mv manually is painful.

Better approaches:

Option 1: Script it

Use:

terraform state list

Then generate state mv commands via script.

=================================================================

Option 2: Use moved blocks (Terraform ≥1.1)

Cleaner way 👇

moved {
  from = aws_vpc.myvpc
  to   = module.network.aws_vpc.myvpc
}

moved {
  from = aws_subnet.subnet1
  to   = module.network.aws_subnet.subnet1
}

👉 This avoids manual state commands and is safer for CI/CD
=====================================================================

if moving some more resources then change the files inside module and also the root module file(values)
